<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The full robustness results of GAT and GraphSAGE are reported in Appendix (Tables <a href="#A6.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ Are LLMs Better GNN Helpers? Rethinking Robust Graph Learning under Deficiencies with Iterative Refinement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A6.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ Are LLMs Better GNN Helpers? Rethinking Robust Graph Learning under Deficiencies with Iterative Refinement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), as a complement to the GCN results shown in the main paper (Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 5.2.3. Robustness under Compound Deficiencies (RQ3) ‣ 5.2. Results and Analysis ‣ 5. Experiments ‣ Are LLMs Better GNN Helpers? Rethinking Robust Graph Learning under Deficiencies with Iterative Refinement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). GRCN and RS-GNN are designed with GCN backbones, hence they are not applicable to GAT, and their GAT results are not reported in Table <a href="#A6.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ Are LLMs Better GNN Helpers? Rethinking Robust Graph Learning under Deficiencies with Iterative Refinement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, we also report the performance curves of GAT and GraphSAGE across Cora, PubMed, and Arxiv datasets in Figure <a href="#A6.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix F Additional Experimental Results ‣ Are LLMs Better GNN Helpers? Rethinking Robust Graph Learning under Deficiencies with Iterative Refinement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. These results complement the GCN robustness curves shown in the main paper (Figure 6).</p>
</div>
